        <a href="/" class="back">← BACK</a>
        <h1>PRIVACY POLICY</h1>
        <p class="updated">Last updated: 17 April 2026</p>

        <h2>WHAT WE COLLECT</h2>
        <p>When you use Dirty Laundry, we collect:</p>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Account information</strong> — Email address, display name, and password (if you create an account). Anonymous users only provide a display name.</li>
          <li><strong>Group data</strong> — Group names, chore names, completion records, points, reactions, and photos you upload as proof of completion.</li>
          <li><strong>Push notification tokens</strong> — If you opt in to push notifications, we store your device's push subscription to send you notifications.</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>WHAT WE DON'T COLLECT</h2>
        <ul>
          <li>We don't track your location</li>
          <li>We don't sell your data to anyone</li>
          <li>We don't use analytics or tracking cookies</li>
          <li>We don't show ads</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>HOW WE USE YOUR DATA</h2>
        <p>Your data is used solely to make the app work:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Display your chores, points, and leaderboard to your group members</li>
          <li>Send push notifications you've opted into (nudges, completions, reactions)</li>
          <li>Calculate reports and statistics for your group</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>WHO CAN SEE YOUR DATA</h2>
        <p>Your data is only visible to members of your group. We don't share your data with advertisers, brokers, or anyone outside your household group.</p>

        <h2>SERVICE PROVIDERS</h2>
        <p>We use a small number of trusted third parties to run the Service. They only process the data they need to do their job, and never use it for their own purposes:</p>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Supabase</strong> — hosts our database, authentication, and file storage (EU region, on AWS).</li>
          <li><strong>Web-push providers</strong> — deliver browser notifications you've opted in to. They only receive the minimum needed to route the message to your device.</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>PHOTOS</h2>
        <p>Photos uploaded as proof of completion are stored in our cloud infrastructure (Supabase Storage). They are accessible to members of your group. You can undo a completion to remove the associated photo.</p>

        <h2>CHILDREN</h2>
        <p>Dirty Laundry supports a "kid" role for children using the app with parental supervision. Kid accounts can be created anonymously (no email required). Parents control the group settings and can remove kid accounts at any time.</p>

        <h2>DATA STORAGE</h2>
        <p>Your data is stored securely on <a href="https://supabase.com">Supabase</a> (hosted on AWS in the EU). Passwords are hashed and never stored in plain text.</p>

        <h2>DELETING YOUR DATA</h2>
        <p>You can leave a group at any time from the group page. To delete your account and all associated data, go to <strong>Profile → Delete Account</strong> in the app. This permanently removes your profile, points, completions, and uploaded photos. If you'd rather we handle it, email <strong>hello@dirtylaundry.club</strong> and we'll sort it within 48 hours.</p>

        <h2>CONTACT</h2>
        <p>Questions about your data? Email <strong>hello@dirtylaundry.club</strong></p>
      </div>
    </div>
